{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "CircleCI Yarn Offline Cache Triage",
    "Explanation": [
      "The frozen step list shows only Spin up environment, Preparing environment variables, Checkout code, and Install Dependencies; there is no restore_cache step, and in config.yml both restore_cache and save_cache are commented out, so no cache was restored in this run (cache_restored: false). The job log explicitly states 'info No lockfile found.', meaning yarn.lock does not exist in the repository, so it cannot be the checksum target; the only shown repository file that declares dependencies is package.json (also hinted by the step names 'Restore/Save Yarn Package Json Cache'), so the cache key should use checksum of package.json. Because --offline must stay and the offline install can only succeed if a populated ~/.cache/yarn is carried between builds, the job needs both the restore_cache step (before install) and the save_cache step (after install) enabled, i.e. enable_restore_and_save_cache."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"cache_restored\": false,",
      "  \"checksum_target\": \"package.json\",",
      "  \"fix\": \"enable_restore_and_save_cache\"",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"cache_restored\": false,",
        "  \"checksum_target\": \"package.json\",",
        "  \"fix\": \"enable_restore_and_save_cache\"",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
