{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "CircleCI deploy job missing branch filter",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow.txt shows workflow build-test-and-deploy finished SUCCESS with all three jobs SUCCESS, so the pipeline is green. However, the run was on branch `koans-08-branch-filters`, not `production`, and the `deploy` job still ran and succeeded. The requirement says `deploy` must run only for commits to `production`, so the behaviour is incorrect. The config has no `filters` on the `deploy` workflow entry; `requires` only orders jobs and does not restrict branches. The fix is to add `filters: branches: only: production` to the `deploy` job's workflow entry (`build` and `test-production` have no restriction requirement, so they should not be changed; ignoring non-production branches would be an inverted/unnecessary approach; filters belong in the workflow entry, not the job definition)."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
