{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "CircleCI parallel test split not applied",
    "Explanation": [
      "The `test` job has `parallelism: 2`. The Run tests command does call `circleci tests split`, and the logs show the split worked (node 0 got src/test_goodbye.sh, node 1 got src/test_hello.sh), but the for loop iterates over the raw glob `src/test_*.sh` instead of the contents of /tmp/split.txt. Consequently both nodes ran both files (\"Ran 2 file(s); split list had 1\") and the guard failed each node with exit 1. So the suite did not actually split (suite_split=false) and every node ran the full suite (each_node_ran_full_suite=true). The fix is to actually consume the `circleci tests split` output in the loop (e.g. iterate over /tmp/split.txt), so each node runs only its assigned files; this keeps parallelism, leaves the workflow untouched, and makes the RAN==EXPECTED check pass."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"each_node_ran_full_suite\": true,",
      "  \"fix\": \"use_circleci_tests_split\",",
      "  \"suite_split\": false",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"each_node_ran_full_suite\": true,",
        "  \"fix\": \"use_circleci_tests_split\",",
        "  \"suite_split\": false",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
