{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "CircleCI Tag Filter Triage for Deploy Job",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow summary shows all three jobs SUCCESS, so the run was green. However, the trigger was an untagged branch push (branch koans-09-tag-filters, no tag) and the deploy job still ran, which violates the requirement that untagged pushes must not deploy; the config has no filters at all, so deploy runs on every push. `requires` alone cannot gate on tags. To meet the full requirement, deploy needs `filters: tags: only: /^beta-.*/` with `branches: ignore: /.*/`. But CircleCI does not run jobs on tag pushes unless they have a tags filter, and a filtered deploy that requires unfiltered build/test would never run (or the workflow would be incomplete) on tag `beta-main-0.1.1`. Therefore build and test must also receive tag filters so the whole chain runs on the beta tag and the workflow is green and deploys. The change is a filters block on the workflow entries of all jobs, restricting tags to beta."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
