{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "CircleCI deploy failure: app paths not persisted",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow summary shows build-linux, build-mac, and build-windows all SUCCESS, so builds_green is true. The deploy job is FAILED (its 'Verify apps present' step exited with code 1), so deploy_green is false. The job.log shows the attached workspace contained only ./meta/\u003cplatform\u003e/build.txt files and none of the app/\u003cplatform\u003e/app.* files, so workspace_had_apps is false. Root cause: each build job's persist_to_workspace only lists meta/\u003cplatform\u003e under paths, never app/\u003cplatform\u003e, so the app files are never carried to deploy. The correct fix is to persist the app paths (app/linux, app/windows, app/mac) from each build job so they are attached in deploy; storing artifacts only on builds would not make them available in deploy, fixing one platform would still fail the other two tests, changing attach_workspace does nothing when the data was never persisted, and removing verification would violate the requirement that deploy verifies presence."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"builds_green\": true,",
      "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
      "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"builds_green\": true,",
        "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
        "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
